course: dictionary
lesson: 15923
title: Unprepared: not ready
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word unprepared is made of three parts: un-, prepare and -ed. The un- at the start means not, so unprepared means not ready. Prepared means ready, so unprepared means not ready for something.
explain: You can use unprepared about a person. «I was unprepared for the spelling test because I had not practised.» This means I was not ready for the test.
explain: You can also use unprepared about a thing that has not been made ready. «The ground was unprepared, so we could not plant the seeds yet.» The ground had not been dug or made ready for planting.
fact: Unprepared means not ready for something.
fact: The un- at the start of a word means not, and prepared means ready.
fact: Unprepared can describe a person, or a thing that has not been made ready, such as unprepared ground.
fact: «Caught unprepared» means something happened when you were not ready for it.
fact: Being prepared helps people stay safe, which is why schools hold fire drills and families keep first aid kits.
exercise: «The sudden storm caught the campers unprepared.» What does unprepared mean here? | *Not ready for the storm | Warm and dry in their tents | Happy to see the rain | Very tired from walking
exercise: Mum says, «We always pack a first aid kit, so we are never unprepared.» Why would a family pack a first aid kit? | To have a picnic on the beach | To make a new friend | *To be ready if someone gets hurt | To make the car heavier
exercise: «Oliver forgot his PE kit, so he was unprepared for the lesson.» Find and copy one word that shows Oliver was not ready. | lesson | *unprepared | forgot | Oliver
test: «Oliver forgot his PE kit, so he was unprepared for the lesson.» What does unprepared mean? | *Not ready, without the kit he needed | Very fast and full of energy | Excited to play in the rain | Happy to sit out and watch
test: «The field was unprepared, so the football match could not start.» What does unprepared mean for a field? | Very wet and muddy | Ready for a race | *Not made ready for play | Covered in flowers
exam: Which meaning fits «caught unprepared»? | Caught a ball in the park | *Taken by surprise, not ready | Found a lost prize | Lost in a busy shop
